The '''Galactic Combat World Championship''' (abbreviated '''GCWC''') is the premier international [[esports]] tournament for ''[[Galactic Combat]]'', the {{w|multiplayer online battle arena|MOBA}} video game developed and published by [[Jocs Importants]]. First held in 2015, the tournament brings together the top-ranked players from each of the game's four competitive regions — Mesogean–Illypnia, North Kaftia–North Fosia, East Fosia, and Lurandia-Abyala — to compete for the world championship title. The GCWC is held annually, typically in September over approximately one week, and is one of the most watched esports events in the world.

== Format ==

The GCWC features sixteen teams — four from each of the four competitive regions — competing over approximately one week in September. The tournament is divided into two stages: a group stage followed by a knockout bracket.

During the group stage, the sixteen teams are divided into four groups of four, with each group containing one team from each region. Teams play a round-robin format within their group, with the top two teams from each group advancing to the knockout stage. The group stage typically occupies the first three days of the tournament.

The knockout stage is a single-elimination bracket consisting of eight teams. Quarterfinals, semifinals, and the grand final are played over the remaining days, with the grand final held on the last day of the tournament. All knockout matches are best-of-five, while the group stage matches are best-of-three.

Qualification for the GCWC is based on performance in the regional leagues that operate throughout the competitive season in each of the four regions. The top four teams from each region's league standings at the end of the season earn invitations to the World Championship.

== History ==

=== Inaugural championship (2015) ===

The first Galactic Combat World Championship was held in September 2015 at the [[Centre de Convencions del Districte Financer]] in the [[Districte Financer (Original, Sant Cristòfor)|Districte Financer]] district of [[Original (ciutat)|Original]], [[Sant Cristòfor]], [[Balboa]]. The inaugural tournament featured sixteen teams from the four competitive regions and was the first major international esports event organised by [[Jocs Importants]]. The prize pool was approximately $500,000, funded primarily by the developer with additional contributions from sponsors. The event was broadcast online and attracted a peak viewership of approximately 1.2 million concurrent viewers.

=== Sant Cristòfor years (2015–2017) ===

The first three editions of the GCWC (2015, 2016, and 2017) were all held at the [[Centre de Convencions del Districte Financer]] in Sant Cristòfor. The choice of venue reflected the game's Balboan origins and the developer's headquarters in nearby [[Dàrsena (ciutat)|Dàrsena]]. The convention center, located in the financial district of Original, provided sufficient capacity for the growing audience and was easily accessible via the city's metro system.

Over these three years, the tournament grew steadily in both prize pool and viewership. The 2016 edition increased the prize pool to approximately $1 million, while the 2017 edition reached approximately $1.5 million. Peak concurrent viewership grew from 1.2 million in 2015 to approximately 2.5 million in 2017.

=== International expansion (2018–2019) ===

Beginning in 2018, the GCWC began rotating host cities to reflect the game's growing international player base. The 2018 championship was held in [[Aoyama]], [[Nakamizu]], marking the first time the tournament was held outside Balboa. The move to Aoyama was motivated by the large and passionate Galactic Combat player base in the Sanese archipelago and the city's modern convention facilities.

The 2019 championship was held in [[Castejón]], [[Balisca]], further expanding the tournament's global reach. The Castejón edition saw the prize pool surpass $3 million for the first time, driven by increased sponsorship and the introduction of community crowdfunding through in-game purchases.

=== Online championship (2020) ===

The 2020 GCWC was held entirely online due to the [[Adonian pandemic]]. The tournament was restructured to accommodate remote play, with teams competing from their respective regions across multiple time zones. The online format presented significant technical challenges, particularly regarding network latency between regions, but the tournament was completed successfully. The prize pool was maintained at approximately $4 million, and the event demonstrated the viability of remote esports competition during a period when in-person events were impossible worldwide.

=== Return to in-person events (2021–2023) ===

The 2021 championship was held in [[Ampuria]], [[Volisania]], marking a return to in-person competition. The Ampuria edition was the largest GCWC to date, with a prize pool exceeding $6 million and peak concurrent viewership surpassing 5 million. The 2021 tournament coincided with the peak of Galactic Combat's player base, which reached 6 million concurrent players that year.

The 2022 championship was held in [[Mazar]], [[Burawa]], reflecting the game's significant Kaftian player base. The 2023 championship was held in [[Klow]], [[Varkana]], continuing the tournament's global rotation.

=== Dàrsena Esports Arena and beyond (2024–present) ===

The 2024 championship was held at the newly constructed [[Dàrsena Esports Arena]] in [[Dàrsena (ciutat)|Dàrsena]], [[Sant Cristòfor]], marking the tournament's return to the game's birthplace. The Dàrsena Esports Arena was built specifically as a dedicated esports venue in the district where [[Jocs Importants]] is headquartered, and its construction was announced in 2022 as part of a broader investment in Balboan esports infrastructure. The 2024 edition featured a prize pool exceeding $10 million, the largest in the tournament's history.

The 2025 championship was held in [[Alsvik]], [[Skade]], continuing the global rotation. The 2026 championship is scheduled to be held from 7 to 12 September in [[Okami]], [[Okaiken]], marking the first time the GCWC will be hosted in the Sanese archipelago since the 2018 Aoyama edition.

